1074:
**γενεά**, -ᾶς, ἡ 
(γίγνομαι), [in LXX chiefly for דּוֹר, דֹּר (Cremer, 148) ;] 
1. **race, stock, family** (in NT, γέννημα, which see). 
2. **generation**; 
(a) **of the contemporary members of a family**: pl., [[40-matthew.1.17|Mat.1:17]] (cf. [[01-genesis.31.3|Gen.31:3]], מוֹלֶדֶת); metaphorically, of those alike in character, in bad sense, [[40-matthew.17.17|Mat.17:17]], [[41-mark.9.19|Mrk.9:19]], [[42-luke.9.41|Luk.9:41 16:8]], [[44-acts.2.40|Act.2:40]]; 
(b) **of all the people of a given period**: [[40-matthew.24.34|Mat.24:34]], [[41-mark.13.30|Mrk.13:30]], [[42-luke.21.32|Luk.21:32]], [[50-philippians.2.15|Php.2:15]]; pl., [[42-luke.1.48|Luk.1:48;]] esp. of the Jewish people, [[40-matthew.11.16|Mat.11:16 12:39, 41 42, 45 16:4 23:36]], [[41-mark.8.12|Mrk.8:12, 38]] [[42-luke.7.31|Luk.7:31 11:29, 30-32, 50, 51 17:25]], [[44-acts.13.36|Act.13:36]], [[58-hebrews.3.10|Heb.3:10]]" (LXX) ; τὴν γ. αὐτοῦ τίς διηγήσεται, [[44-acts.8.33|Act.8:33]] (LXX); 
(with) the period covered by the life-time of a generation, used loosely in pl. of successive ages: [[44-acts.14.16|Act.14:16 15:21]], [[49-ephesians.3.5|Eph.3:5]], [[51-colossians.1.26|Col.1:26]]; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ. (= לִדוֹר וָדוֹר, al.), [[42-luke.34.17|Luk.34:17]], al), [[42-luke.1.50|Luk.1:50;]] εἰς πάσας τὰς γ. τοῦ αἰῶνος τῶν αἰώνων, [[49-ephesians.3.21|Eph.3:21]] (Ellic, in l.; _DCG_, i, 639f.).
(AS)

