1106:
**γνώμη**, -ης, ἡ 
(γιγνώσκω), [in LXX: [[27-daniel.2.15|Da TH 2:15]] (דָּת), [[19-psalms.83.3|Ps 82(83):3]] (סוֹד), elsewhere, chiefly II Es, for טְעֵם ;] 
1. **a means of knowing, a token** (Theogn.). 
2. In Attic writers, **the mind**, its operations and results (see Edwards, _Lex._, _App._, A); 
(a) **mind, understanding**; 
(b) **purpose, intention**: [[44-acts.20.3|Act.20:3;]] 
(with) **judgment, opinion**: [[46-1-corinthians.1.10|1Co.1:10]], [[66-revelation.17.13|Rev.17:13]]; 
(d) **counsel, advice**: [[46-1-corinthians.7.25|1Co.7:25, 40]] [[47-2-corinthians.8.10|2Co.8:10]], Phm 14; 
(e) **royal purpose, decree** (as in Da, I and II Es): [[66-revelation.17.17|Rev.17:17]] (Cremer, 671).
(AS)

1121:
**γράμμα**, -τος, τό 
(γράφω), [in LXX for סֵפֶר, etc. ;] 
1. **that which is traced** or **drawn, a picture**. 
2. **that which is written**; 
(1) **a character, letter**: [[48-galatians.6.11|Gal.6:11;]] 
(2) **a writing, a written document**; 
(a) **a bill** or **account**: [[42-luke.16.6|Luk.16:6]], 7; 
(b) **a letter**: [[44-acts.28.21|Act.28:21;]] 
(with) τὰ ἱερὰ γ., **the sacred writings**, i.e. the OT: [[55-2-timothy.3.15|2Ti.3:15]] (so in Philo, _Vit. Mos._, iii, 39) ; 
(d) τὸ γ., **the letter**, the written word as an external authority in contrast with the direct influence of the Spirit as manifested in the new Covenant: [[45-romans.2.27|Rom.2:27, 29 7:6]], [[47-2-corinthians.3.6|2Co.3:6]], 7; 
(3) τὰ γ., **letters**, i.e. **learning**: [[43-john.7.15|Jhn.7:15]], [[44-acts.26.24|Act.26:24]]. (In π. an illiterate person is very frequently referred to as γράμματα μ᾽̀ εἰδότης, and this "never means anything else than inability to write": MM, _Exp._, x; but see also Cremer, 166; _DCG_, i, 202; ii, 584.)
(AS)

1125:
**γράφω**, [in LXX chiefly for כּתב ]; 
1. **to scrape, graze** (Hom.), and later (Hdt.) **to sketch, draw**. 
2. **to write**; 
(a) **of forming or tracing letters on writing material**: Jhn.8:[6], [[48-galatians.6.11|Gal.6:11]], [[53-2-thessalonians.3.17|2Th.3:17]]; 
(b) **to express in writing, commit to writing, record**: [[42-luke.1.63|Luk.1:63]], [[43-john.19.21|Jhn.19:21, 22]] [[66-revelation.1.11|Rev.1:11, 19]] al.; of scripture as a standing authority (Deiss., _BS_, 112ff.), γέγραπται, **it stands written** (Luther), [[40-matthew.4.4|Mat.4:4]], [[41-mark.7.6|Mrk.7:6]], [[42-luke.4.8|Luk.4:8]], [[45-romans.1.17|Rom.1:17]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.31|1Co.1:31]], al.; id. before ἐν, [[41-mark.1.2|Mrk.1:2]], [[44-acts.1.20|Act.1:20]], al.; with accusative, **to write of**: [[43-john.1.46|Jhn.1:46]], [[45-romans.10.5|Rom.10:5]]; before περί, [[40-matthew.26.24|Mat.26:24]], [[41-mark.14.21|Mrk.14:21]], [[43-john.5.46|Jhn.5:46;]] al.; with dative (WM, §31, 4), [[42-luke.18.31|Luk.18:31;]] id. before ἵνα (M, _Pr._, 207f.), [[41-mark.12.19|Mrk.12:19]], [[42-luke.20.28|Luk.20:28]]; κατὰ τ. γεγραμμένον, [[47-2-corinthians.4.13|2Co.4:13;]] γεγραμμένον ἐστί, [[43-john.2.17|Jhn.2:17;]] ἐγράφη, [[45-romans.4.24|Rom.4:24;]] ἐπ᾽ αὐτῷ γεγραμμένα, [[43-john.12.16|Jhn.12:16;]] 
(with) of writing directions or information, with dative of person(s): [[45-romans.15.15|Rom.15:15]], [[47-2-corinthians.7.12|2Co.7:12]], al.; 
(d) **of that which contains the record or message**: βιβλίον, [[41-mark.10.4|Mrk.10:4]], [[43-john.21.25|Jhn.21:25]], [[66-revelation.5.1|Rev.5:1]]; τίτλον, [[43-john.19.19|Jhn.19:19;]] ἐπιστολήν, [[44-acts.23.25|Act.23:25;]] ἐντολήν, [[41-mark.10.5|Mrk.10:5]] (cf. ἀπο-, ἐγ-, ἐπι-, κατα-, προ-).
(AS)

1140:
**δαιμόνιον**, -ου, τό
(neut. of δαιμόνιος, -α, -ον, _divine_), [in LXX (so also in π; see MM, _Exp._, x) for שֵׁד, אֱלִיל, (frequently in To) ;] 
1. as in cl.; 
(a) **the Divine power, Deity** (Hdt., Plat., al.); 
(b) **an inferior divinity, deity** or **demon** (as in magical π, Deiss., _BS_, 281; MM, _Exp._, x): ξένα δ., [[44-acts.17.18|Act.17:18.]] 
2. (a) in OT, heathen deities, false gods (e.g. [[05-deuteronomy.32.17|Deu.32:17]], Psa.95 (96):5); 
(b) in NT, **evil spirits, demons**: θύουσιν δαιμονίοις, [[46-1-corinthians.10.20|1Co.10:20;]] διδασκαλίαι δαιμονίων, [[54-1-timothy.4.1|1Ti.4:1;]] προσκυνεῖν τὰ δ., [[66-revelation.9.20|Rev.9:20;]] ἄρχων τῶν δ., [[40-matthew.9.34|Mat.9:34;]] especially (syn. with πνεῦμα ἀκάθαρτον) as operating upon and "possessing" (of. δαιμονίζομαι) men: [[40-matthew.11.18|Mat.11:18]], and al.; εἰσέρχεσθαι δ. εἰς. . ., [[42-luke.8.30|Luk.8:30;]] δ. ἔχειν, [[42-luke.4.33|Luk.4:33;]] δ. ἐκβάλλειν, [[40-matthew.7.22|Mat.7:22]] In the phrase πνεῦμα δαιμονίου ἀκαθάρτου, [[42-luke.4.33|Luk.4:33]], the wider cl. usage (1. _b_) is recognised, ἀκ. being elsewhere in NT, the epithet of πν., and δ. = πν. ἀκ. (see _ICC_, in l; Cremer, 168) 
(AS)

1166:
**δείκνυμι**, δεικνύω (see Bl., § 23, 1; Veitch, see word), 
[in LXX chiefly for רָאָה hi. ;] 
**to show**, with accusative of thing(s) (of person(s)), dative of person(s); 
(a) **to show, exhibit**: [[40-matthew.4.8|Mat.4:8 8:4]], [[41-mark.1.44|Mrk.1:44 14:15]], [[42-luke.4.5|Luk.4:5 5:14 20:24 22:12 24:40]], [[43-john.2.18|Jhn.2:18 5:20 10:32; 20:20]] [[44-acts.7.3|Act.7:3]]" (LXX), [[54-1-timothy.6.15|1Ti.6:15]], [[66-revelation.17.1|Rev.17:1 21:9, 10 22:1, 8]], pass., [[58-hebrews.8.5|Heb.8:5]] (LXX); 
(b) **to make known**: [[40-matthew.16.21|Mat.16:21]], [[43-john.14.8|Jhn.14:8]], 9, [[44-acts.10.28|Act.10:28]], [[46-1-corinthians.12.31|1Co.12:31]], [[66-revelation.1.1|Rev.1:1 4:1 22:6]]; 
(with) **to prove**: [[59-james.2.18|Jas.2:18 3:13]].
(AS)

1175:
**δεισιδαιμονία**, -ας, ἡ 
