1189:
**δέομαι** 
(mid. of δέω, II, which see, as depon.) [in LXX for חנן, etc. ;] 
**to want for oneself**; 
1. **to want, need**: 
(a) absol.; 
(b) with genitive 
2. **to beg, request, beseech, pray**; 
(i) **in general**: absol., [[44-acts.26.3|Act.26:3]], WH; with genitive of person(s), [[42-luke.5.12|Luk.5:12; 8:28; 38]] (ἐδεῖτο; T, ἐδέετο, cf. Veitch, see word δέω) 9:38, [[44-acts.8.34|Act.8:34; 21:39]], [[47-2-corinthians.5.20|2Co.5:20]], [[48-galatians.4.12|Gal.4:12]]; before ἵνα, [[42-luke.9.40|Luk.9:40;]] before τό, with inf., [[47-2-corinthians.10.2|2Co.10:2;]] with genitive of person(s) and of thing(s), [[47-2-corinthians.8.4|2Co.8:4;]] 
(ii) **of prayer to God**: absol., [[44-acts.4.31|Act.4:31;]] before εἴ πως, [[45-romans.1.10|Rom.1:10;]] ἵνα, [[42-luke.21.36|Luk.21:36; 22:32]]; εἰς τό, [[52-1-thessalonians.3.10|1Th.3:10;]] ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ πρὸς τ. κύριον, ὅπως, [[44-acts.8.24|Act.8:24;]] with genitive, τοῦ κυρίου, ὅπως, [[40-matthew.9.38|Mat.9:38]], [[42-luke.10.2|Luk.10:2]]; τοῦ Θεοῦ, [[44-acts.10.2|Act.10:2;]] before εἰ ἄρα, [[44-acts.8.22|Act.8:22.]] 
_SYN._: αἰτέω, and cf. δέησις. (AS)

1219:
**δημόσιος**, -α, -ον
(δῆμος), [in LXX: 2Ma.6:10, 3Ma.2:27 4:7 * ;] 
