1223:
**διά** (before a vowel δ᾽, exc. [[45-romans.8.10|Rom.8:10]], [[47-2-corinthians.5.7|2Co.5:7]], and in (Proper name)s; Tdf., _Pr._, 94), 
_prep. with genitive, accusative, as in cl.; _ 
1. with genitive, **through**; 
(i) **of Place, after verbs of motion or action**: [[40-matthew.2.12|Mat.2:12 12:43]], [[41-mark.2.23|Mrk.2:23]], [[42-luke.4.30|Luk.4:30]], [[43-john.4.4|Jhn.4:4]], [[47-2-corinthians.11.33|2Co.11:33]], al.; σώζεσθαι (διας-) δ. πυρός, ὕδατος, [[46-1-corinthians.3.15|1Co.3:15]], [[60-1-peter.3.20|1Pe.3:20]]; βλέπειν δ. ἐσόπτρου, [[46-1-corinthians.13.12|1Co.13:12;]] metaphorically, of a state or condition: [[45-romans.14.20|Rom.14:20]], [[47-2-corinthians.2.4|2Co.2:4 5:7]], 10; δ. γράμματος, ἀκροβυστίας (Lft., _Notes_, 263, 279), [[45-romans.2.27|Rom.2:27 4:11]]; δι ̓ὑπομενῆς, [[45-romans.8.25|Rom.8:25.]] 
(ii) **Of Time**; 
(a) **during which**: [[40-matthew.26.61|Mat.26:61]], [[41-mark.14.58|Mrk.14:58]], [[42-luke.5.5|Luk.5:5]]; δ. παντὸς τοῦ ζῆν, [[58-hebrews.2.15|Heb.2:15;]] δ. παντός (διαπαντός in [[41-mark.5.5|Mrk.5:5]], [[42-luke.24.53|Luk.24:53]]), **always, continually**, [[40-matthew.18.10|Mat.18:10]], [[44-acts.2.25|Act.2:25]]" (LXX) 10:2 24:16, [[45-romans.11.10|Rom.11:10]]" (LXX), [[53-2-thessalonians.3.16|2Th.3:16]], [[58-hebrews.9.6|Heb.9:6 13:15]]. 
(b) **within which**: [[44-acts.1.3|Act.1:3;]] δ. νυκτός, [[44-acts.5.19|Act.5:19 16:9 17:10 23:31]]; 
(with) **after which **(Field, _Notes_, 20; Abbott, _JG_, 255f.): [[41-mark.2.1|Mrk.2:1]], [[44-acts.24.17|Act.24:17]], [[48-galatians.2.1|Gal.2:1]]. 
(iii) **Of the Means or Instrument**; 
(1) **of the efficient cause **(regarded also as the instrument): of God, [[45-romans.11.36|Rom.11:36]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.9|1Co.1:9]], [[48-galatians.4.7|Gal.4:7]], [[58-hebrews.2.10|Heb.2:10 7:21]]; of Christ, [[45-romans.1.8|Rom.1:8 5:1, 17]], [[46-1-corinthians.15.21|1Co.15:21]], [[60-1-peter.4.11|1Pe.4:11]], al.; δ. τ. ὑμῶν δεήσεως, [[45-romans.1.12|Rom.1:12]], [[47-2-corinthians.1.4|2Co.1:4]], [[48-galatians.4.23|Gal.4:23]], al.; 
(2) **of the agent, instrument or means**; 
(a) with genitive of person(s), [[40-matthew.11.2|Mat.11:2]], [[42-luke.1.70|Luk.1:70]], [[43-john.1.17|Jhn.1:17]], [[44-acts.1.16|Act.1:16]], [[45-romans.2.16|Rom.2:16]], [[46-1-corinthians.1.21|1Co.1:21]], [[49-ephesians.1.5|Eph.1:5]], [[58-hebrews.2.14|Heb.2:14]], [[66-revelation.1.1|Rev.1:1]], al.; ὑπὸ τ. κυρίου δ. τ. προφήτου (δ. τ. κυρίου, [[52-1-thessalonians.4.2|1Th.4:2]] (M, _Th._, in l.); Lft., _Rev._, 121f.), [[40-matthew.1.22|Mat.1:22 2:15]], [[45-romans.1.2|Rom.1:2]]; δ. ἐπιστολῆς ὡς δ. ἡμῶν (Field, _Notes_, 202), [[53-2-thessalonians.2.2|2Th.2:2;]] δ. Σ. (_NTD_, 22), [[60-1-peter.5.12|1Pe.5:12;]] 
(b) with genitive of thing(s) (where often the simple dative is used in cl.; Jannaris, _Gr._, 375), [[43-john.11.4|Jhn.11:4]], [[44-acts.5.12|Act.5:12]]; δ. τ. πίστεως, [[45-romans.3.30|Rom.3:30;]] δ. λόγου θεοῦ, [[60-1-peter.1.23|1Pe.1:23;]] δ. παραβολῆς, [[42-luke.8.4|Luk.8:4;]] δουλεύειν δ. τ. ἀγάπης, [[48-galatians.5.13|Gal.5:13;]] δ. ἐπαγγελίας, [[48-galatians.3.18|Gal.3:18]], 
2. C. accusative; 
(i) rarely, as with genitive, **through** (Hom), δ. μέσον Σαμαρίας (ICC, in l.; Bl., §42, 1; Robertson, _Gr._, 581), [[42-luke.17.11|Luk.17:11.]] 
(ii) **by reason of, because of, for the sake of**; 
(a) with accusative of person(s) (M, _Pr._, 105), [[41-mark.2.27|Mrk.2:27]], [[43-john.6.57|Jhn.6:57 11:42]], [[45-romans.8.20|Rom.8:20]]; 
(b) with accusative of thing(s), δ. φθόνον, [[40-matthew.27.18|Mat.27:18]], [[41-mark.15.10|Mrk.15:10]]; δ. φόβον, [[43-john.7.13|Jhn.7:13 20:19]]; δ. ἀγάπην, [[49-ephesians.2.4|Eph.2:4;]] δ. τοῦτο, freq., **for this cause, therefore**, [[40-matthew.6.25|Mat.6:25]], [[41-mark.6.14|Mrk.6:14]], [[42-luke.11.49|Luk.11:49]], [[43-john.6.65|Jhn.6:65]], al.; id. before ὅτι, [[43-john.5.16|Jhn.5:16 10:17]], al.; δ. τί, **why**, [[40-matthew.9.11|Mat.9:11, 14]] [[41-mark.2.18|Mrk.2:18]], [[43-john.7.45|Jhn.7:45]], al.; δ. τό, with inf., [[41-mark.5.4|Mrk.5:4]], [[42-luke.9.7|Luk.9:7]], [[59-james.4.2|Jas.4:2]]. 
3. In composition, 
(1) **through**, as in διαβαίνω; 
(2) of separation, **asunder**, as in διασπάω; 
(3) of distribution, **abroad**, as in διαγγέλλω; 
(4) **of transition, as διαλλάσσω**; 
(5) of "perfective" action (M, _Pr._, 112f., 115f.), as διαφύγω, διακαθαρίζω. 
(AS)

1228:
**διάβολος**, -ον
(διαβάλλω, which see) [in LXX for שָׂטָן (as [[18-job.1.6|Job.1:6]]), exc. [[17-esther.7.4|Est.7:4 8:1]] (צַר, צָרַר) ;] 
**slanderous, accusing falsely**. As subst., ὁ, ἡ, δ.; 
(a) generally (of. Es, ll. with), **a slanderer, false accuser**: [[54-1-timothy.3.6|1Ti.3:6]], 7 (CGT, in l., but see infr.) 3:11, [[55-2-timothy.3.3|2Ti.3:3]], [[56-titus.2.3|Tit.2:3]]; 
(b) **as chiefly in LXX, of Satan, the Accuser, the Devil**: [[40-matthew.4.1|Mat.4:1, 5, 8, 11 13:39 25:41]], [[42-luke.4.2|Luk.4:2, 3, 6, 13 8:12]], [[43-john.13.2|Jhn.13:2]], [[44-acts.10.38|Act.10:38]], [[49-ephesians.4.27|Eph.4:27 6:11]], [[54-1-timothy.3.6|1Ti.3:6]], 7 (but see supr.), [[55-2-timothy.2.26|2Ti.2:26]], [[58-hebrews.2.14|Heb.2:14]], [[59-james.4.7|Jas.4:7]], [[60-1-peter.5.8|1Pe.5:8]], Ju 9, [[66-revelation.2.10|Rev.2:10 12:9, 12 20:2, 10]]; εἶναι ἐκ τοῦ δ., [[43-john.8.44|Jhn.8:44]], [[62-1-john.3.8|1Jn.3:8]]; τέκνα τοῦ δ., [[62-1-john.3.10|1Jn.3:10;]] υἱὸς, [[44-acts.13.10|Act.13:10;]] metaphorically, of Judas, [[43-john.6.70|Jhn.6:70]] (Cremer, 121; _DCG_, ii, 605).
(AS)

1329:
**δι-ερμηνεύω **
[in LXX: 2Ma.1:36 * ;] 
intensive of ἐρμηνεύω, **to interpret**; 
(a) **to explain, expound**: with accusative, [[42-luke.24.27|Luk.24:27;]] absol., [[46-1-corinthians.12.30|1Co.12:30 14:5 14:13 14:27]]; 
(b) **to translate**: [[44-acts.9.36|Act.9:36.]]
(AS)

1411:
**δύναμις**, -εως, ἡ 
(δύναμαι), [in LXX for עֹז ,גּבוּרָה ,צָבָה ,(חֵיל) חַיִל, etc.; 35 words in all ;] 
**power, might, strength**; relatively, **ability, power** to perform: [[40-matthew.25.15|Mat.25:15]], [[44-acts.3.12|Act.3:12]], [[58-hebrews.11.11|Heb.11:11]]; κατὰ δ., [[47-2-corinthians.8.3|2Co.8:3;]] παρὰ δ., ib.; ὑπὲρ δ., [[47-2-corinthians.1.8|2Co.1:8;]] of pecuniary ability, [[47-2-corinthians.8.3|2Co.8:3]], [[66-revelation.18.3|Rev.18:3]]; absol., **power, might**: [[42-luke.24.49|Luk.24:49]], [[44-acts.1.8|Act.1:8]]; opposite to ἀσθένεια, [[46-1-corinthians.15.43|1Co.15:43;]] ἡ δ. τ. ἁμαρτίας, [[46-1-corinthians.15.56|1Co.15:56;]] of power in action, [[45-romans.1.16|Rom.1:16, 20]] [[46-1-corinthians.1.18|1Co.1:18]], [[50-philippians.3.10|Php.3:10]], al.; ἡ δ. τ. θεοῦ, [[40-matthew.22.29|Mat.22:29]], [[41-mark.12.24|Mrk.12:24]], [[45-romans.1.20|Rom.1:20]], al.; opposite to μόρφωσις, [[55-2-timothy.3.5|2Ti.3:5;]] in doxologies, [[66-revelation.4.11|Rev.4:11 7:12]], al.; ἐν δ., [[41-mark.9.1|Mrk.9:1]], [[42-luke.4.36|Luk.4:36]], [[45-romans.1.4|Rom.1:4]], al.; of the power of performing miracles, [[44-acts.6.8|Act.6:8]], [[53-2-thessalonians.2.9|2Th.2:9]]; pl., [[40-matthew.13.54|Mat.13:54]], [[41-mark.6.14|Mrk.6:14]], [[48-galatians.3.5|Gal.3:5]], al.; of the **force** or **meaning** of a word (Plat., al.), [[46-1-corinthians.14.11|1Co.14:11.]] By meton., of persons or things; 
(a) of God, [[40-matthew.26.64|Mat.26:64]], [[41-mark.14.62|Mrk.14:62]] (Dalman, _Words_, 200ff.); 
(b) of angels, [[45-romans.8.38|Rom.8:38]], [[49-ephesians.1.21|Eph.1:21]], [[60-1-peter.3.22|1Pe.3:22]]; 
(with) of armies, pl. [LXX for צְבָאוֹת ], metaphorically, of the stars, [[40-matthew.24.29|Mat.24:29]], [[41-mark.13.25|Mrk.13:25]], [[42-luke.21.26|Luk.21:26]]; 
(d) of that wh. manifests God's power: Christ, [[46-1-corinthians.1.24|1Co.1:24;]] τ. εὐαγγέλλιον, [[45-romans.1.16|Rom.1:16;]] ἡ δ. τ. κυρίου, [[46-1-corinthians.5.4|1Co.5:4;]] 
(e) of mighty works (Tr., _Syn._, §xci), δ. ποιεῖν, [[41-mark.6.5|Mrk.6:5 9:39]]; pl., [[40-matthew.7.22|Mat.7:22]], [[41-mark.6.2|Mrk.6:2]], [[42-luke.10.13|Luk.10:13]], al.; σημεῖακ. δ., [[44-acts.8.13|Act.8:13;]] δ. κ. τέρατα κ. σημεῖα, [[44-acts.2.22|Act.2:22]], [[47-2-corinthians.12.12|2Co.12:12]]. 
_SYN._: βία, ἐνέργεια, ἐξουσία, ἰσχύς, κράτος (see Tr., l.with; Cremer, 218, 236; _DB_, i, 616; iv, 29; _DCG_, i, 607; ii, 188). (AS)

1437:
**ἐάν**, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν, 
_conditional particle_, 
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. [[43-john.13.17|Jhn.13:17]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.36|1Co.7:36]]), **if haply, if**; 
1. with subjc. (cl.); 
(a) pres.: [[40-matthew.6.22|Mat.6:22]], [[42-luke.10.6|Luk.10:6]], [[43-john.7.17|Jhn.7:17]], [[45-romans.2.25|Rom.2:25, 26]] al.; 
{ (b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): [[40-matthew.4.9|Mat.4:9 16:26]] (cf. ptcp. in [[42-luke.9.25|Luk.9:25;]] M, _Pr._, 230), [[41-mark.3.24|Mrk.3:24]], [[42-luke.14.34|Luk.14:34]], [[43-john.5.43|Jhn.5:43]], [[45-romans.7.2|Rom.7:2]], al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., [[43-john.9.22|Jhn.9:22 11:57]], [[44-acts.9.2|Act.9:2]]; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, [[43-john.12.32|Jhn.12:32 14:3]], I [[43-john.2.28|Jhn.2:28 3:2]], [[58-hebrews.3.7|Heb.3:7]]" (LXX) . 
2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, _App._, 171; VD, _MGr._ 2, _App._, §77; Deiss., _BS_, 201f., _LAE_, 155, 254; M, _Pr._, 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4); 
(a) fut.: [[40-matthew.18.19|Mat.18:19]] T, [[42-luke.19.40|Luk.19:40]], [[44-acts.7.7|Act.7:7;]] 
(b) pres.: [[52-1-thessalonians.3.8|1Th.3:8]] (see Milligan, in l.). 
3. **With other particles**: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), [[48-galatians.6.1|Gal.6:1;]] ἐ. μή (M, _Pr._, 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., [[40-matthew.10.13|Mat.10:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.8.8|1Co.8:8]], [[59-james.2.17|Jas.2:17]], [[62-1-john.3.21|1Jn.3:21;]] aor., [[40-matthew.6.15|Mat.6:15]], [[41-mark.3.27|Mrk.3:27]], [[43-john.3.3|Jhn.3:3]], [[45-romans.10.15|Rom.10:15]], [[48-galatians.1.8|Gal.1:8 2:16]] (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, [[17-esther.19.13|Est.19:13]], al.,] [[45-romans.14.8|Rom.14:8]]. 
4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., _Pr._, 96; WH, _App._, 173; M, _Pr._, 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., _BS_, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., [[40-matthew.5.19|Mat.5:19]], [[41-mark.6.22|Mrk.6:22, 23]] [[42-luke.17.32|Luk.17:32]], [[46-1-corinthians.6.18|1Co.6:18]], al.; ὅπου ἐ., [[40-matthew.8.19|Mat.8:19;]] ὁσάκις ἐ., [[66-revelation.11.6|Rev.11:6;]] οὗ ἐ., [[46-1-corinthians.16.6|1Co.16:6;]] καθὸ ἐ., [[47-2-corinthians.8.12|2Co.8:12;]] ὅστις ἐ., [[48-galatians.5.10|Gal.5:10.]] 
(AS)

1438:
**ἑαυτοῦ**, -ῆς, -οῦ, dative -ῷ, etc., accusative -όν, etc., pi. -ῶν, etc. (Att. contr. αὑτοῦ, etc); 
_reflex pron._; 
1. prop, of 3rd person (Lat. sui, sibi, se), **of himself, herself, itself**, etc.: [[40-matthew.27.42|Mat.27:42]], [[41-mark.15.31|Mrk.15:31]], [[42-luke.23.35|Luk.23:35]], al.; added to a middle verb, διεμερίσαντο ἑαυτοῖς, [[43-john.19.24|Jhn.19:24;]] to an active verb, [[44-acts.14.14|Act.14:14]] (M, _Pr._, 157); ἀφ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[42-luke.12.57|Luk.12:57 21:30]], [[43-john.5.19|Jhn.5:19]], al. (see: ἀπό); δι᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[45-romans.14.14|Rom.14:14;]] ἐν ἑ., [[40-matthew.3.9|Mat.3:9]], [[41-mark.5.30|Mrk.5:30]], al.; εἰς ἑ., [[42-luke.15.17|Luk.15:17;]] καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, [[44-acts.28.16|Act.28:16]], [[59-james.2.17|Jas.2:17]]; παρ᾽ ἑαυτῷ, **at his own house**, [[46-1-corinthians.16.2|1Co.16:2;]] πρὸς ἑ., **with, to himself**, [[42-luke.18.11|Luk.18:11;]] as poss. pron. (with emphasis weakened; see M, _Pr._, 87f.), τ. ἑαυτῶν νεκρούς, [[42-luke.9.60|Luk.9:60.]] 
2. As reflexive 1st and 2nd of person(s) (so also frequently in cl., chiefly poetry), [[40-matthew.23.31|Mat.23:31]], [[41-mark.9.50|Mrk.9:50]], [[45-romans.8.23|Rom.8:23]], [[52-1-thessalonians.2.8|1Th.2:8]], al. 
3. In pl., for reciprocal pron., ἀλλήλων, -οις, -ους, **of one another**, etc.: [[40-matthew.21.38|Mat.21:38]], [[41-mark.16.3|Mrk.16:3]], [[49-ephesians.5.19|Eph.5:19]], al. 
(AS)

1506:
**εἰλικρινής**, -ές, 
[in LXX: Wi 72^ kB * ;] 
**unalloyed, pure** (Lat. sincerus; see _DCG_, ii, 635a); 
(a) **of unmixed substances**; 
(b) **of abstract ideas**; 
(with) **of ethical purity**: [[50-philippians.1.10|Php.1:10]], [[61-2-peter.3.1|2Pe.3:1]].
_SYN._: ἁγνός (which see), καθαρός, cf. Tr., _Syn._: §lxxxv; _DB_, iv, 176a; Cremer, 378; Westc. on [[62-1-john.3.3|1Jn.3:3.]] (AS)

1519:
**εἰς**, 
_prep. with accusative, _ 
expressing entrance, direction, limit, **into, unto, to, upon, towards, for, among** (Lat. in, with accusative). 
I. Of place. 
1. After verbs of motion; 
(a) **of entrance into**: [[40-matthew.8.23|Mat.8:23, 9:7]], [[41-mark.1.45|Mrk.1:45]], [[42-luke.2.15|Luk.2:15, 8:31]], al.; 
(b) of approach, **to** or **towards**: [[41-mark.11.1|Mrk.11:1]], [[42-luke.6.8|Luk.6:8, 19:28]], [[43-john.11.31|Jhn.11:31, 21:6]], al.; 
(with) before pl. and collective nouns, **among**: [[41-mark.4.7|Mrk.4:7, 8:19, 20]], [[42-luke.11.49|Luk.11:49]], [[43-john.21.23|Jhn.21:23]], al.; 
(d) Of a limit reached, **unto, on, upon**: [[40-matthew.8.18|Mat.8:18, 21:1]], [[41-mark.11.1|Mrk.11:1, 13:16]], [[42-luke.14.10|Luk.14:10]], [[43-john.6.3|Jhn.6:3, 11:32]], al.; with accusative of person(s) (as in Ep. and Ion.), [[44-acts.23.15|Act.23:15]], [[45-romans.5.12|Rom.5:12, 16:19]], [[47-2-corinthians.10.14|2Co.10:14]]; 
(e) **elliptical**: ἐπιστολαὶ εἰς Δαμασκόν, [[44-acts.9.2|Act.9:2;]] ἡ διακονία μου ἡ εἰς Ἱ., [[45-romans.15.31|Rom.15:31;]] metaphorically, of entrance into a certain state or condition, or of approach or direction towards some end (Thayer, B, i, 1; ii, 1), εἰς τ. ὄνομα, M, _Pr._, 200. 
2. Of direction; 
(a) **after verbs of seeing**: [[40-matthew.6.26|Mat.6:26]], [[41-mark.6.41|Mrk.6:41]], [[42-luke.9.16|Luk.9:16, 62]], [[43-john.13.22|Jhn.13:22]], al.; metaphorically, of the mind, [[58-hebrews.11.26|Heb.11:26, 12:2]], al.; 
(b) **after verbs of speaking**: [[40-matthew.13.10|Mat.13:10, 14:9]], [[52-1-thessalonians.2.9|1Th.2:9]], al.
3. After verbs of rest; 
(a) **in "pregnant" construction, implying previous motion **(cl.; see WM, 516; Bl., §39, 3; M, _Pr._, 234f.): [[40-matthew.2.23|Mat.2:23, 4:13]], [[53-2-thessalonians.2.4|2Th.2:4]], [[55-2-timothy.1.11|2Ti.1:11]], [[58-hebrews.11.9|Heb.11:9]], al.; 
(b) by an assimilation general in late Gk (see Bl., M, _Pr._, ll. with) = ἐν: [[42-luke.1.44|Luk.1:44, 4:23]], [[44-acts.20.16|Act.20:16, 21:17]], [[43-john.1.18|Jhn.1:18]] (but see Westc, in l.), al. 
II. Of time, **for, unto**; 
1. accentuating the duration expressed by the accusative: εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, [[40-matthew.21.19|Mat.21:19;]] εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ., [[42-luke.1.50|Luk.1:50;]] εἰς τ. διηνεκές, [[58-hebrews.7.3|Heb.7:3]], al. 
2. Of a point or limit of time, **unto, up to, until**: [[40-matthew.6.34|Mat.6:34]], [[44-acts.4.3|Act.4:3, 25:21]], [[50-philippians.1.10|Php.1:10, 2:16]], [[52-1-thessalonians.4.15|1Th.4:15]], [[55-2-timothy.1.12|2Ti.1:12]]; of entrance into a future period, σεις τὸ μέλλον (see: μέλλω), **next (year)**, [[42-luke.13.9|Luk.13:9]] (but with _ICC_, in l.); εἰς τ. μεταξὺ σάββατον, **on the next Sabbath**, [[44-acts.13.42|Act.13:42;]] εἰς τὸ πάλιν (see: πάλιν, [[47-2-corinthians.13.2|2Co.13:2.]] 
III. Of result, after verbs of changing, joining, dividing, etc.: στρέφειν εἰς, [[66-revelation.11.6|Rev.11:6;]] μετας-, [[44-acts.2.20|Act.2:20]], [[59-james.4.9|Jas.4:9]]; μεταλλάσσειν, [[45-romans.1.26|Rom.1:26;]] σχίζειν εἰς δύο, [[40-matthew.27.51|Mat.27:51]], al.; predicatively with εἴναι, [[44-acts.8.23|Act.8:23.]] 
IV. Of relation, **to, towards, for, in regard to** (so in cl., but more frequently in late Gk., εἰς encroaching on the simple dative, which it has wholly displaced in MGr.; Jannaris, _Gr._, §1541; Robertson, _Gr._, 594; Deiss., _BS_, 117f.): [[42-luke.7.30|Luk.7:30]], [[45-romans.4.20|Rom.4:20, 15:2, 26]], [[46-1-corinthians.16.1|1Co.16:1]], [[49-ephesians.3.16|Eph.3:16]], al.; ἀγάπη εἰς, [[45-romans.5.8|Rom.5:8]], al.; χρηστός, [[49-ephesians.4.32|Eph.4:32;]] φρονεῖν εἰς, [[45-romans.12.16|Rom.12:16;]] θαρρεῖν, [[47-2-corinthians.10.1|2Co.10:1.]] 
V. **Of the end or object**: εὔθετος εἰς, [[42-luke.14.34|Luk.14:34;]] σόφος, [[45-romans.16.19|Rom.16:19;]] ἰσχύειν, [[40-matthew.5.13|Mat.5:13;]] εἰς τοῦτο, [[41-mark.1.38|Mrk.1:38]], al.; ἀφορίζειν εἰς, [[45-romans.1.1|Rom.1:1;]] indicating purpose, εἰς φόβον, [[45-romans.8.15|Rom.8:15;]] εἰς ἔνδειξιν, [[45-romans.3.25|Rom.3:25;]] εἰς τό, with inf. (= ἵνα or ὥστε; Bl., §71, 5; M, _Pr._, 218ff.): [[40-matthew.20.19|Mat.20:19]], [[45-romans.1.11|Rom.1:11]], [[46-1-corinthians.9.18|1Co.9:18]], al. 
VI. **Adverbial phrases**: εἰς τέλος, εἰς τὸ πάλιν, etc (see: τέλος, πάλιν, etc.).
(AS)

1520:
**εἷς **
ιά, ἕν, genitive ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός, 
cardinal numeral, **one**; 
1. **one**, as opposite to many: [[40-matthew.25.15|Mat.25:15]], [[45-romans.5.12|Rom.5:12]], [[46-1-corinthians.10.8|1Co.10:8]], al.; as subst., [[45-romans.5.15|Rom.5:15]], [[49-ephesians.2.14|Eph.2:14]]; id. with genitive partit., [[40-matthew.5.19|Mat.5:19]], al.; before ἐκ (ἐξ), [[41-mark.14.18|Mrk.14:18]], [[43-john.6.8|Jhn.6:8]], al.; metaphorically, of union and concord, [[43-john.10.30|Jhn.10:30 17:11]], [[45-romans.12.4|Rom.12:4-5]], [[50-philippians.1.27|Php.1:27]]; ἀπὸ μιᾶς (B1., § 44, 1), [[42-luke.14.18|Luk.14:18;]] with neg., εἷς. . . οὐ (μή), more emphatic than οὐδείς, no one, none (cl.), [[40-matthew.5.18|Mat.5:18 10:29]], [[42-luke.11.46|Luk.11:46 12:6]]. 
2. Emphatically, to the exclusion of others; 
(a) **a single (one)**: [[40-matthew.21.24|Mat.21:24]], [[41-mark.8.14|Mrk.8:14]]; absol., [[46-1-corinthians.9.24|1Co.9:24]], al.; οὐδὲ εἷς, [[40-matthew.27.14|Mat.27:14]], [[43-john.1.3|Jhn.1:3]], [[45-romans.3.10|Rom.3:10]], al.; 
(b) **one, alone**: [[41-mark.2.7|Mrk.2:7 10:18]], [[42-luke.18.19|Luk.18:19]]; 
(with) **one and the same**: [[45-romans.3.30|Rom.3:30]], [[46-1-corinthians.3.8|1Co.3:8 11:5 12:11]], [[62-1-john.5.8|1Jn.5:8]]. 
3. In late Gk., with weakened force, = τις or indef. art. (of. _Heb._ אֶחָד, [[01-genesis.22.13|Gen.22:13]], al.; see B1., § 45, 2; M, _Pr._, 96 f.): [[40-matthew.8.19|Mat.8:19 19:6]], [[66-revelation.8.13|Rev.8:13]], al.; εἷς τις (Bl., l.with), [[42-luke.22.50|Luk.22:50]], [[43-john.11.49|Jhn.11:49]] 
4. **Distributively**: εἷς καστος (cl.), [[42-luke.4.40|Luk.4:40]], [[44-acts.2.6|Act.2:6]], al.; εἷς . . . καὶ εἷς (cl., εἷς μὲν . . . εἷς δέ), [[40-matthew.17.4|Mat.17:4]], [[41-mark.9.5|Mrk.9:5]], [[43-john.20.12|Jhn.20:12]], al. (cf. LXX and use of _Heb._ אֶחָד, [[02-exodus.17.12|Exo.17:12]], al); ὁ εἷς . . . ὁ ἕτερος (ἄλλος) = cl. ὁ μὲν (ἕτερος) . . . ὁ δέ (ἕτερος), [[40-matthew.6.24|Mat.6:24]], [[42-luke.7.41|Luk.7:41]], [[66-revelation.17.10|Rev.17:10]]; καθ᾽ εἷς, εἷς κ. είς (in which καθ᾽ is adverbial, or the expression formed from the analogy of ἕν καθ᾽ ἔν; M, _Pr._, 105), **one by one, severally**: [[41-mark.14.19|Mrk.14:19]], [[45-romans.12.5|Rom.12:5]], al.; εἷς τὸν ἕνα = ἀλλήλους (B1., 45, 2; M, _Pr._, 246), [[52-1-thessalonians.5.11|1Th.5:11.]] 
